(go/type trie "A trie[V] maps keys to values V, similar to a map.\nA key is a list of integers; two keys collide if one of them is a prefix of the other.\nFor instance, [1, 2] and [1, 2, 3] collide, but [1, 2, 3] and [1, 2, 4] do not.\nIf all keys have length 1, a trie degenerates into an ordinary map[int]V.\n" :type-params [V] (map int any)) ; map value is either trie[V] (non-leaf node), or V (leaf node)







